      "content": "<h3>4. firstKey, lastKey, firstEntry and lastEntry</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Signature:</strong> <code>K firstKey();  K lastKey();  Map.Entry<K, V> firstEntry();  Map.Entry<K, V> lastEntry()</code></li>\n<li><strong>Returns:</strong> the key / the entry</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> O(log n)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For freshers:</strong> <code>firstKey()</code> and <code>lastKey()</code> return the smallest and the largest <strong>key</strong> and throw <code>NoSuchElementException</code> when the map is empty. <code>firstEntry()</code> and <code>lastEntry()</code> return the whole <strong>pair</strong> (or <code>null</code> when empty).</p>\n<p><strong>For experienced developers:</strong> The entry versions are safer for possibly-empty maps and give the value in the same call. The returned entries are snapshots: calling <code>setValue</code> on them throws <code>UnsupportedOperationException</code>.</p>",
