      "content": "<h3>5. pollFirstEntry() and pollLastEntry()</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Signature:</strong> <code>Map.Entry<K, V> pollFirstEntry();  Map.Entry<K, V> pollLastEntry()</code></li>\n<li><strong>Returns:</strong> the removed entry, or <code>null</code> if empty</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> O(log n)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For freshers:</strong> Remove and return the entry with the smallest or the largest key. Repeat <code>pollFirstEntry</code> until it returns <code>null</code> to process entries in key order while consuming them (a sorted queue with lookups).</p>\n<p><strong>For experienced developers:</strong> Handy for event schedulers: key = time, value = task; <code>pollFirstEntry</code> always gives the next task due.</p>",
